<title>SINGAPORE: QAF proposes rights issue.</title>
<headline>QAF proposes rights issue.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Food-based QAF Ltd said on Tuesday it was proposing a renounceable rights issue with warrants to raise between Singapore $2.0-2.2 billion to finance its acquisition of PT Indofood Sukses Makamur.  </p>
<p>QAF said in a statement it would issue up to 2.21 billion rights shares at Singapore $1 each with free detachable warrants. The issue is on the basis of five rights for every one QAF share.</p>
<p>QAF shares were last traded at Singapore $1.80 before its suspension effective July 11, 1997, pending an announcement.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
